  "articleBody": "When you're dreaming up your tiny home, it's easy to overlook some key things that can make a big difference in how livable the space feels. Avoiding these common pitfalls can save you headaches down the road! \n\n- **Forgetting about storage from the start** — Many people design their layout and then try to squeeze in storage. Instead, integrate clever storage solutions like under-floor compartments, built-in shelves, and multi-functional furniture from day one. You'd be amazed how much can be tucked away without feeling cluttered. \n\n- **Ignoring how you actually live** — Don't just copy a pretty picture from Pinterest. Think about your real daily habits: how often do you cook? Do you work from home? Do you host guests? Your layout needs to support *your* lifestyle, not a hypothetical one. \n\n- **Overlooking natural light and ventilation** — Small spaces can feel claustrophobic without enough light and fresh air. Strategically placed windows and proper ventilation aren't just aesthetic; they're crucial for comfort and well-being. \n\n- **Choosing bulky furniture** — Standard-sized furniture can quickly overwhelm a tiny space. Opt for scaled-down pieces, custom-built solutions, or items designed specifically for small living. \n\n- **Not considering the ",
